Here's a program that takes two command line arguments, a string and a positive odd integer, and prints out each character in the string the number of times specified by the integer, following the pattern you described:

```java
public class PatternPrinting {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        if (args.length != 2) {
            System.out.println("Please provide a string and a positive odd integer as command line arguments.");
            return;
        }

        String inputString = args[0];
        int oddInteger = Integer.parseInt(args[1]);

        if (oddInteger <= 0 || oddInteger % 2 == 0) {
            System.out.println("Please provide a positive odd integer.");
            return;
        }

        int previousAsciiValue = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < inputString.length(); i++) {
            char c = inputString.charAt(i);
            int repetitions = i + previousAsciiValue + 1;

            for (int j = 0; j < repetitions; j++) {
                System.out.print(c);
            }

            previousAsciiValue = (int) c;
        }
    }
}
```

