import java.util.Scanner;

public class RightTriangle {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Get the base of the triangle from the user
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter the base of the right triangle: ");
        int base = scanner.nextInt();

        StringBuilder triangleBuilder = new StringBuilder();
        int number = 1;

        // Generate the right triangle pattern in a single loop
        for (int i = 1; i <= base; i++) {

            // Generate the number sequence for this row
            StringBuilder rowBuilder = new StringBuilder();
            for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
                rowBuilder.append(number).append(" ");
                number += 2;
            }

            // Add spaces to center align the number sequence
            int spaces = base - i;
            StringBuilder spacesBuilder = new StringBuilder();
            for (int j = 1; j <= spaces; j++) {
                spacesBuilder.append(" ");
            }

            // Add this row to the triangle
            triangleBuilder.append(spacesBuilder).append(rowBuilder).append("\n");
        }

        // Print the right triangle pattern
        System.out.println(triangleBuilder.toString());
    }

}
```

This optimized version uses a single loop to generate the entire triangle pattern. Each row is generated as a separate String with StringBuilder for efficient string concatenation, then appended to the whole triangle string. The triangle string is then printed all at once. This reduces the time complexity from O(n^2) to O(n), and keeps the space complexity at O(n).

