Here is a Java program to find and delete all duplicate elements in an array:

```java
import java.util.Arrays;

public class RemoveDuplicates {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] array = {1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 5, 3, 6, 7, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 5};

        // Sort the array
        Arrays.sort(array);

        // Initialize variables
        int j = 0;

        // Iterate through the array
        for (int i = 0; i < array.length - 1; i++) {
            // If current element is not equal to the next element, copy it to the result
            if (array[i] != array[i + 1]) {
                array[j] = array[i];
                j++;
            }
        }

        // Copy the last element to the result
        array[j] = array[array.length - 1];

        // Create a new array with the unique elements
        int[] result = Arrays.copyOfRange(array, 0, j + 1);

        // Print the result
        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(result));
    }
}
```

This program uses the `Arrays.sort()` method to sort the array in ascending order. Then, it iterates through the array and copies each unique element to a new array. Finally, it prints the new array without any duplicate elements.

