Write a JavaScript program to take a multi-dimensional array of numbers, flatten it, and return a single-dimensional array in which each element is the result of squaring the original values. Additionally, solve this problem without using any built-in JavaScript array flattening functions like .flat() or .reduce(). 

Given an erroneous piece of code below, identify the errors and fix them.

```javascript
function squareArray(arr) {
  let result = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (typeof arr[i] === 'object') {
      squareArray(arr[i]);
    } else {
      result.push(arr[i] * arr[i]);
    }
  }
  return result;
}
console.log(squareArray([[1, 2], [3, 4]]));  // Expected Output : [1, 4, 9, 16]
res = []

