```java
public static int findKthSmallest(int[] array, int k) {
    if (array == null || array.length == 0 || k <= 0 || k > array.length) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid input");
    }

    int left = 0;
    int right = array.length - 1;

    while (true) {
        int pivotIndex = partition(array, left, right);

        if (pivotIndex == k - 1) {
            return array[pivotIndex];
        } else if (pivotIndex > k - 1) {
            right = pivotIndex - 1;
        } else {
            left = pivotIndex + 1;
        }
    }
}

private static int partition(int[] array, int left, int right) {
    int pivot = array[right];
    int i = left - 1;

    for (int j = left; j < right; j++) {
        if (array[j] <= pivot) {
            i++;
            swap(array, i, j);
        }
    }

    swap(array, i + 1, right);

    return i + 1;
}

private static void swap(int[] array, int i, int j) {
    int temp = array[i];
    array[i] = array[j];
    array[j] = temp;
}
```

This implementation uses the Quickselect algorithm, which is a modified version of the QuickSort algorithm. It selects a pivot element and partitions the array around the pivot, such that all elements smaller than the pivot are placed before it and all elements larger than the pivot are placed after it. By repeating this process recursively, the algorithm is able to find the kth smallest element in linear time on average.

The `findKthSmallest` method first checks for any invalid input and initializes the left and right pointers. Then, it enters a while loop that continues until the kth smallest element is found. In each iteration, the `partition` method is called to partition the array based on a pivot element. If the pivot index is equal to k - 1, then the kth smallest element has been found and it is returned. If the pivot index is greater than k - 1, then the kth smallest element must be in the left partition, so the right pointer is updated. If the pivot index is less than k - 1, then the kth smallest element must be in the right partition, so the left pointer is updated.

The `partition` method takes the array, left and right pointers as parameters. It selects the pivot element as the last element in the array. It then initializes the i pointer to the left - 1 position. It iterates over the array from left to right - 1 using the j pointer. If the current element is smaller than or equal to the pivot, then the i pointer is incremented and the current element is swapped with the element at the i position. This ensures that all elements smaller than or equal to the pivot are placed before it. Finally, the pivot element is swapped with the element at the i + 1 position, placing it in its correct sorted position. The pivot index is then returned.

The `swap` method is a utility method that swaps two elements in the array.

