print(p.yes()) # True
print(p.not_yes()) # False
print(p.maybe(True)) # True
print(p.not_maybe(True)) # False
```

In this code, each lambda function now has its own personal v, which doesn't change when the loop variable v changes. Now the code should work as expected.

