- The time complexity of the `Arrays.sort()` method is `O(n log n)`. However, the overall complexity of the implementation stays relatively efficient and doesn't cross `O(n log n)`, assuming that string preprocessing cleanups take linear time.
- This methodology is based on comparing sorted versions of the input strings. If they are anagrams, their sorted versions will be equal.
- I've implemented this as part of a class called `AnagramChecker` for logical organization, but it could just as easily be a static utility function, depending on the larger program context.

