Using this function, you can encode a JSON object into a query string. The `encodeURIComponent` function is used to encode both keys and values to make sure they are accurately represented in the resulting query string. The array "map" function is used to transform each key-value pair into a string of the form "key=value", and the "join" function then joins all these strings together using the "&" character.

As an extension and to handle nested objects:

```javascript
function jsonToQueryString(json) {
    return Object.keys(json).map(function(key) {
        if (typeof json[key] === 'object') {
            return Object.keys(json[key]).map(function(subKey) {
                return encodeURIComponent(key) + '[' + encodeURIComponent(subKey) + ']=' + encodeURIComponent(json[key][subKey]);
            }).join('&');
        } else {
            return encodeURIComponent(key) + '=' + encodeURIComponent(json[key]);
        }
    }).join('&');
}
```

In the above code, the function checks whether each value is an object (nested). If it is, it will join each sub-key with an equal sign and the corresponding sub-value and wrap it with the main key. The end result here is to transform every object or nested object into string format in the form of a query string.

