3. Least privilege principle: Ensure that the database user used by the web application has the least privilege necessary to perform its tasks. Limit the user's permissions to only the required tables and operations. By doing so, even if an attacker manages to inject malicious SQL code, the damage will be limited. Erroneous code example without least privilege principle:

